# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version automatically selected by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the body element, after the Providers wrapper
- Followed Next.js App Router (v13.5+) best practices as specified in the documentation

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was placed in the root layout file as recommended for Next.js App Router projects. This ensures:
- Speed Insights is active on all pages
- Minimal performance overhead
- Proper integration with Next.js routing

The component is placed after the main content (children wrapped in Providers) but before the closing body tag, following standard practice for analytics and monitoring tools.

## Verification

✅ TypeScript compilation: Passed
✅ ESLint: No errors
✅ Next.js build: Compiled successfully (TypeScript verification completed)
✅ Lock file updated: package-lock.json properly synchronized

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance data
2. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights
3. Metrics typically appear within a few days of user visits

## Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package resolution
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
